{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrierBarParity","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.sum_c4_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.sum_c4_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPTwoTermSum.lean#L222-L258","doc":"**The quartic rung satisfies `c₄ ≤ −4/5`.** From\n`c₄·w⁴ = t − c₃·w³ ≤ 24/10⁸ − (1/5)·(108/10000)³ = −11942.4/10¹²` against\n`w⁴ ≤ (11/1000)⁴`. So the small-height band available to `c₄` is `[−5, −4/5]`,\nnot `[−5, −1/5] ∪ [1/5, 5]`. Margin `0.0956 %`.\n\n**`−4/5` is content, not slack.** The sharp window-wide bound is `−0.8156820`,\nso `−4/5` leaves `0.01568`; a mutation to `−82/100` fails to close. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.sum_c3_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.sum_c3_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPTwoTermSum.lean#L176-L220","doc":"**The cubic rung is pinned to `[1/5, 1/4]`.** The lower bound is the\nsmall-height hypothesis once the sign is known; the upper bound is\n`c₃·w³ = t − c₄·w⁴ ≤ 24/10⁸ + 5·(11/1000)⁴`, against `w³ ≥ (108/10000)³`. The\nmargin is genuine but thin — `313205/10¹²` against `314928/10¹²`, `0.5471 %` —\nso it is exact rational arithmetic, not a decimal estimate.\n\n**`1/4` is content, not slack.** The sharp window-wide bound is\n`313205/1259712 = 0.2486322`, so `1/4` leaves `0.00137`; a mutation to `24/100`\nfails to close. Stated because a reader cannot otherwise tell a chosen round\nnumber from a forced one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.sum_signs_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.sum_signs_forced","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPTwoTermSum.lean#L97-L169","doc":"**The two-term bar-even tail must alternate.** If `c₃·w³ + c₄·w⁴ = t` with\nboth coefficients of small height, `q` in the pin window and `t` in the residual\nwindow, then `c₃` is positive and `c₄` is negative.\n\n**It is stronger than its signature.** Only `1/5 ≤ |c₃|` and `|c₄| ≤ 5` are\nused — `_hc31` and `_hc40` are carried so the three theorems in this file take\nthe same hypotheses and compose without plumbing. **The check that establishes\nthis is deleting both binders and fixing the two positional call sites: the\nproof closes unchanged.** Do *not* reach for the unused-variable linter here;\n`linter.unusedVariables` does not fire on a binder prefixed with `_`, so its\nsilence on this signature is the underscore doing its job and says nothing\neither way. (An earlier version of this docstring cited that silence as the\nevidence. The claim was true and the evidence was not: a reviewer who checked\nit as invited would have seen nothing and been unable to tell \"unused\" from\n\"warning suppressed\". Caught by an independent verification pass.)\n\nSo the alternation holds for a quartic coefficient of *arbitrarily small*\nheight and for a cubic coefficient of *arbitrarily large* height;\nsmall-heightness is needed only as a floor on `|c₃|` and a ceiling on `|c₄|`.\nDo not read the extra binders as required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.wGen_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPTwoTermSum.wGen_pos","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPTwoTermSum.lean#L82-L87","doc":"`w > 0` on the pin window. ","signatureChunk":0}]}